.TH SPARKY-STEREO-THEME-EDITOR 1 "2026-11-16" "0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sparky-stereo-theme-editor \- edit icon and theme projects with a stereo preview
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sparky-stereo-theme-editor
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Select named SVG parts, set their depth within the desktop limits, inspect
per-size pixel disparities, and save a separate theme project copy.
The source theme stays read only. Undo and redo change the project in memory.
The preview supplies both views to Stereo KWin, which chooses each display's output.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--project " folder
Open a previously saved project.
.TP
.BI "--theme " folder
Open an icon theme. Use --icon to choose its SVG source.
.TP
.BI "--icon " file
Choose the SVG or SVGZ source inside the icon theme.
.TP
.BI "--places " file
Load group depths from JSON. Values range from -1 to 1 within the desktop limits.
.TP
.BI "--save " folder
Save to a new project folder. An existing destination is refused.
.TP
.B --flat
Disable the stereo preview.
.TP
.B --exit-after-save
Exit after the requested operation.
.TP
.B --help
Show command help.
.SH FILES
A saved project contains project.json, its copied icon theme under icons,
and marked stereo raster derivatives under pairs.
